---
import Layout from "@/layouts/main.astro"

const repo = "https://github.com/kylemclaren/jevql"
const install = "brew install kylemclaren/tap/jevql"
---

<Layout>
  <main class="page">
    <header class="mast">
      <a class="brand" href="./">jevql</a>
      <div class="mast-right">
        <span class="tagline">Semantic SQL for vanilla Postgres</span>
        <a class="repo-link" href={repo} aria-label="GitHub repository">
          <svg class="gh" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27.68 0 1.36.09 2 .27 1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.013 8.013 0 0 0 16 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8Z"/></svg>
          GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">A psql-shaped CLI · no Postgres extension required</p>
      <h1>Ask your database <mark>a real question.</mark></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Write <code>WHERE jev(people, 'could work from home')</code>. jevql runs the SQL on Postgres,
        judges the rows with TypeSafe's Jev model, and prints a psql table. Nothing to install on the server,
no <code>CREATE EXTENSION</code>, nothing to ask your DBA for: Postgres only ever sees plain SQL.
      </p>
      <div class="truth-strip">
        <span>works on any postgres</span><span>no extension</span><span>no proxy</span><span>answers cached</span><span>$0.042 / M tokens</span>
      </div>
      <div class="install-cta">
        <button id="download" type="button">
          <span class="material-symbols-rounded" aria-hidden="true">download</span> download jevql
        </button>
        <button id="copy-install" class="secondary" type="button" data-copy={install}>
          <span class="material-symbols-rounded" aria-hidden="true">content_copy</span> {install}
        </button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <dialog id="dl" aria-labelledby="dl-title">
      <div class="dl-head">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">download</p><h2 id="dl-title">Pick your platform</h2></div>
        <button id="dl-close" class="secondary" type="button" aria-label="Close">✕</button>
      </div>
      <p class="dl-version">latest release: <strong id="dl-tag">…</strong></p>
      <div class="dl-grid" id="dl-grid">
        <a data-os="darwin" data-arch="arm64" href={`${repo}/releases/latest`}><small>macOS</small><strong>Apple Silicon</strong><span>arm64</span></a>
        <a data-os="darwin" data-arch="amd64" href={`${repo}/releases/latest`}><small>macOS</small><strong>Intel</strong><span>x86_64</span></a>
        <a data-os="linux" data-arch="amd64" href={`${repo}/releases/latest`}><small>Linux</small><strong>x86_64</strong><span>amd64</span></a>
        <a data-os="linux" data-arch="arm64" href={`${repo}/releases/latest`}><small>Linux</small><strong>ARM</strong><span>arm64</span></a>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">Tarball with the <code>jevql</code> binary. Unpack it somewhere on your PATH. Checksums are on the <a href={`${repo}/releases/latest`}>release page</a>. Or <code>brew install kylemclaren/tap/jevql</code>.</p>
    </dialog>

    <section class="race" aria-label="Example query and result">
      <article class="lane direct">
        <div class="lane-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">you type</p><h2>SQL, with one new function</h2></div><span class="badge">query</span></div>
        <pre class="output">SELECT name, city,
       jev_prob(people, 'could work from home') AS p
FROM people
WHERE jev(people, 'could work from home')
  AND country = 'PT'
ORDER BY p DESC
LIMIT 20;</pre>
      </article>
      <article class="lane generated">
        <div class="lane-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">you get</p><h2>A table, and the bill</h2></div><span class="badge pink">result</span></div>
        <pre class="output">     name      |  city  |  p
---------------+--------+------
 Miguel Costa  | Lisbon | 0.94
 Ada Fernandes | Lisbon | 0.93
 Pedro Martins | Lisbon | 0.91
(3 rows)

jev: 6 judged, 1 req, 0 cache hits, 1.2k tokens, $0.0001, 1.35s</pre>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="method-map" aria-label="How a query runs">
      <div><small>1 / collect</small><strong>Postgres runs your SQL with the jev terms stripped. Indexed filters stay on the server.</strong></div>
      <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
      <div class="method-model"><small>2 / judge</small><strong>Surviving rows go to TypeSafe in batches. Identical rows are judged once and cached.</strong></div>
      <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
      <div><small>3 / project</small><strong>Filter, sort, group and limit happen in the CLI. You get a psql table.</strong></div>
    </section>

    <section class="machine" aria-labelledby="functions-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">functions</p><h2 id="functions-title">Same names as pg-jev</h2></div>
        <a class="repo-link" href={`${repo}#sql-surface`}>full surface ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="phases" aria-label="Functions">
        <div class="phase"><small>boolean</small><strong>jev()</strong><span><code>jev(p, 'condition' [, 0.7])</code><br />a calibrated probability against a threshold. Works in WHERE, also as NOT jev().</span></div>
        <div class="phase"><small>numbers</small><strong>jev_prob() jev_score()</strong><span><code>jev_prob(p, 'condition')</code> → 0..1<br /><code>jev_score(p, 'q', ARRAY['lo','mid','hi'])</code> → weighted index</span></div>
        <div class="phase"><small>labels</small><strong>jev_choice()</strong><span><code>jev_choice(t, 'which team?', ARRAY['billing','technical'])</code><br />works with GROUP BY and count(*).</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">Send fewer columns with <code>jev((name, bio), '…')</code>. Anything without <code>jev_*</code> passes straight through, so it doubles as a plain psql.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="machine" aria-labelledby="install-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">install</p><h2 id="install-title">One binary, then just type <code>jevql</code></h2></div>
        <a class="repo-link" href={`${repo}/releases`}>releases ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="phases" aria-label="Install options">
        <div class="phase"><small>homebrew</small><pre class="output">brew install kylemclaren/tap/jevql</pre></div>
        <div class="phase"><small>go</small><pre class="output">CGO_ENABLED=1 go install \
  github.com/kylemclaren/jevql/cmd/jevql@latest</pre></div>
        <div class="phase"><small>binaries</small><pre class="output">macOS arm64 · x86_64
Linux amd64 · arm64</pre></div>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">First launch asks for a database URL and a TypeSafe key and saves them to <code>~/.config/jevql/env</code>. Or use <code>DATABASE_URL</code>, <code>PG*</code> and <code>TYPESAFE_API_KEY</code> like any psql user.</p>
    </section>

    <details>
      <summary>Read before pointing it at real data</summary>
      <div class="details-grid">
        <p><b>Row contents go to TypeSafe.</b> Every column of the judged alias is sent over HTTPS. Narrow it with <code>jev((name, bio), …)</code> or <code>--columns</code>.</p>
        <p><b>It scans everything your SQL filters let through.</b> Put cheap predicates first. <code>--explain</code> shows the collect SQL, row count and cost with no API call; <code>--max-rows</code> aborts before HTTP.</p>
        <p><b>Not an extension.</b> <code>jev()</code> exists only inside this CLI. Apps sending it through JDBC will fail. The names mirror pg-jev, so moving later is a rename.</p>
        <p><b>The cache is a local sqlite file.</b> Keyed by model, question and canonical row JSON. Mode 0600, no expiry. <code>\cache clear</code> or <code>--no-cache</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <footer>
      <span>jevQL · MIT</span>
      <span><a href={repo}>GitHub</a> · <a href="https://typesafe.ai">TypeSafe</a> · <a href="https://github.com/realZachi/pg-jev">pg-jev</a> · styled after <a href="https://github.com/TheoLeeCJ/openjev">openjev</a></span>
    </footer>
  </main>

  <script>
    const dl = document.getElementById("dl") as HTMLDialogElement | null
    const open = document.getElementById("download")
    const close = document.getElementById("dl-close")
    const tagEl = document.getElementById("dl-tag")
    const repo = "https://github.com/kylemclaren/jevql"
    let loaded = false
    async function loadRelease() {
      if (loaded) return
      loaded = true
      try {
        const r = await fetch("https://api.github.com/repos/kylemclaren/jevql/releases/latest", { headers: { Accept: "application/vnd.github+json" } })
        if (!r.ok) throw new Error(String(r.status))
        const rel = await r.json()
        const tag: string = rel.tag_name
        const ver = tag.replace(/^v/, "")
        if (tagEl) tagEl.textContent = tag
        for (const a of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>("#dl-grid a")) {
          const name = `jevql_${ver}_${a.dataset.os}_${a.dataset.arch}.tar.gz`
          const asset = (rel.assets || []).find((x: { name: string }) => x.name === name)
          a.href = asset ? asset.browser_download_url : `${repo}/releases/download/${tag}/${name}`
        }
      } catch {
        if (tagEl) tagEl.textContent = "see releases page"
      }
    }
    // Preselect the visitor's platform.
    const ua = navigator.userAgent
    const guessOS = /Mac/i.test(ua) ? "darwin" : /Linux/i.test(ua) ? "linux" : ""
    const guessArch = /arm64|aarch64/i.test(ua) ? "arm64" : "amd64"
    document.querySelector(`#dl-grid a[data-os="${guessOS}"][data-arch="${guessArch}"]`)?.classList.add("likely")
    open?.addEventListener("click", () => { loadRelease(); dl?.showModal() })
    close?.addEventListener("click", () => dl?.close())
    dl?.addEventListener("click", (e) => { if (e.target === dl) dl.close() })

    const btn = document.getElementById("copy-install")
    if (btn) {
      const original = btn.innerHTML
      btn.addEventListener("click", async () => {
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(btn.dataset.copy || "")
          btn.innerHTML = '<span class="material-symbols-rounded" aria-hidden="true">check</span> copied'
          setTimeout(() => (btn.innerHTML = original), 1400)
        } catch {}
      })
    }
  </script>
</Layout>

<style is:global>
  code { font: inherit; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-weight: 800; }
  .lede code { font-size: .9em; }
  .install-cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 26px; }
  .install-cta button { text-transform: none; }
  button.secondary { background: #fff; }
  button.secondary:hover { background: var(--lime); }
  dialog { position: fixed; inset: 0; margin: auto; max-height: calc(100vh - 40px); overflow: auto; width: min(560px, calc(100% - 28px)); border: 1.5px solid var(--ink); border-radius: 0; background: var(--panel); color: var(--ink); padding: 22px; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 var(--ink); font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; }
  dialog::backdrop { background: rgba(23, 23, 21, .55); }
  .dl-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; gap: 16px; }
  .dl-head h2 { margin: 0; font: 900 1.6rem/1 Arial, sans-serif; letter-spacing: -.045em; }
  .dl-head button { padding: 8px 10px; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--ink); }
  .dl-version { margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: .68rem; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .dl-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 10px; margin-top: 14px; }
  .dl-grid a { display: block; border: 1.5px solid var(--ink); background: #fff; padding: 13px; color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .dl-grid a:hover { background: var(--lime); }
  .dl-grid a.likely { box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 var(--ink); }
  .dl-grid small { display: block; margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: .58rem; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .dl-grid strong { display: block; font-size: .95rem; }
  .dl-grid span { display: block; margin-top: 4px; color: var(--muted); font-size: .62rem; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .dl-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .mast .repo-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; }
  .lane .output { margin: 14px 0 0; border: 0; padding: 0; }
  .method-map { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; }
  .method-map strong { font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.45; }
  .phase .output { margin: 8px 0 0; padding: 0; border: 0; font-size: .66rem; white-space: pre-wrap; }
  .phase strong { font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .phase span code { font-weight: 800; }
  .section-head h2 code { font: inherit; }
  @media (max-width: 750px) { .method-map { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
